<title>USA: Weekend box office chart -- Dec 20-22.</title>
<headline>Weekend box office chart -- Dec 20-22.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final data for the top 10 movies at the December 20-22 box office, according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    Film		   Three-day gross    Cumulative Gross</p>
<p>1. Beavis and Butt-head Do America</p>
<p>				$20,114,233	 $  ----</p>
<p> 2. Jerry Maguire	 $13,125,660	 $36,287,093</p>
<p> 3. 101 Dalmatians	 $6,989,334	 $84,779,528</p>
<p> 4. Scream		   $6,354,586	 $  ----</p>
<p> 5. One Fine Day	   $6,226,430	 $  ----</p>
<p> 6. The Preacher's Wife  $5,182,161	 $15,287,167</p>
<p> 7. Mars Attacks!	  $4,674,116	 $16,655,376</p>
<p> 8. Jingle All the Way   $3,144,864	 $47,405,964</p>
<p> 9. My Fellow Americans  $2,860,334	 $  ----</p>
<p> 10.Daylight		 $2,437,750	 $20,398,315</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Beavis and Butt-head Do America&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc.  &quot;Jerry Maguire&quot; is released by TriStar Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp . &quot;101 Dalmatians&quot; and &quot;The Preacher's Wife&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co.  &quot;Scream&quot; is released by Miramax Films, a unit of Disney. &quot;One Fine Day&quot; and &quot;Jingle All the Way&quot; are released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp .  &quot;Mars Attacks!&quot; and &quot;My Fellow Americans&quot; are released by Warner Bros, a unit of Time Warner Inc. &quot;Daylight&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co Ltd.</p>
